**Worksheet**

F1: mulberry32 rng used everywhere (map, events, trade, storm); endTurn() calls updateProduction→updateColonists→updateCooldowns→checkAshstorm→updateTrade→fireEvent in fixed order. Score 2.

F2: 8x8 map loop; terrain from rng() in initMap; canBuild checks tile.terrain===btype.terrain; calcAdjacencyBonus sets b.productivity, multiplied in updateProduction. Score 2.

F3: greenhouse consumes water to produce food; storage caps via resourceCaps+storage_1; overflow logged and clamped. Score 2.

F4: skillLevel read in updateProduction (skillBonus); fatigue only affects morale in updateColonists, never read by production formula directly. Score 1.

F5: popConsumption subtracted each turn; handleShortage() lowers colonist.morale on shortfall; moraleMult multiplies productivity; unassigned colonists regain morale (+5/turn). Score 2.

F6: 8 research nodes with prereq/cost checks; farming_1, mining_1, storm_1, storage_1, water_1 effects applied in code, but power_1, labor_1, automation have no call site anywhere outside definition. Score 1.

F7: 10 eventDeck entries, weighted pick in fireEvent, cooldown via eventCooldown/updateCooldowns; only 3 events (trade_opportunity, labor_strike, research_insight) have `choices`, short of required 4. Score 1.

F8: caravanPrices formula reads globalDemand (drifts via rng each caravan turn) and player resources[res] stockFactor; tradeWithCaravan handles both selling/buying with capped caravanInventory. Score 2.

F9: checkAshstorm scales severity with turn, damages b.health; updateProduction multiplies productivity by b.health/100; storm_1 research reduces damage; repairBuilding spends parts to restore health. Score 2.

F10: saveToTextarea serializes full state to JSON textarea; loadFromTextarea JSON.parse in try/catch with alert on parse failure, but no field-level validation. Score 1.

F11: win check (turn>=60 && pop>=12 && food/water>=50) and lose check (colonists.length===0) both reachable; endGame() computes score from pop/research/resources/turn and renders end-game-modal. Score 2.

F12: tab-button click handlers switch panels; log-turn span shows entry.turn; tile-tooltip/building-cost show number sources; keydown handles Space + digit-key tab shortcuts; @media rules adapt layout. Score 2.

F13: runTests() has 15 assertions on real invariants (caps, morale/fatigue ranges, prereqs, worker exclusivity); runBenchmark() loops 200 turns calling core functions directly (no UI), computeStateHash() prints hash. Score 2.

G1: research.researchDone.has('farming_1') checked inline in updateProduction to add food bonus — hardcoded per-node special case, not a generic modifier read. Score 2.

G2: handleShortage() writes c.morale on food/water shortfall; updateColonists recomputes avgMorale; updateProduction reads avgMorale via moraleMult every turn. Score 4.

G3: checkAshstorm() sets b.health; updateProduction multiplies productivity by b.health/100; repairBuilding() spends parts and restores health to 100, visible via .damaged class/tooltip. Score 4.

G4: caravanPrices formula reads globalDemand (drifted by rng each caravan turn) and resources[res] via stockFactor; updated every 6 turns, shown in renderTrade. Score 4.

G5: trade_opportunity/labor_strike/research_insight choice effects mutate resources/morale differently per branch, not just logged. Score 4.

